Preheat your oven to 350. Pull out as many #ramekins{} as needed for baking.

Place the @butter{½%cup}(room temperature) and @packed brown sugar{¾%cups} in a #stand mixer{} fitted with a #paddle attachment{}. Beat on medium-high speed until light and fluffy, ~{4%minutes}. Add @large egg{1}(room temperature) and @vanilla{2%teaspoons} and mix again.

Slowly mix in @baking powder{½%teaspoon}, @baking soda{½%teaspoon}, @salt{½%teaspoon} and @all-purpose flour{1½%cups} being careful not to over mix. I usually stop when I still have some flour remnants around the bowl.

Chop up the @milk chocolate{¾%cup}(chopped) bar into chunks, trying to keep some large and some small for different variants of melty chocolate puddles. Stir the chocolate chunks and @semi sweet chocolate chips{½%cup} into the dough until combined.

Scoop the dough into large balls, I like to use the #¼ cup cookie or{} #ice cream scoop{}. Place a single cookie dough ball in a #ramekin{} (mine are 8 oz) or small #pie tin{}. Place all the ramekins on a #cookie sheet{} to easily put in and out of the oven.

Bake the pizookies for ~{16-18%minutes} or until a light golden brown around the edges. Allow to cool until the ramekins are warm, or you can comfortably hold with your hands.

Top each cookie with a scoop of @ice cream{}.
